{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion","id":1525060,"title":"Supernatural Cultists of the Gods of Chaos [Discussion]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-05T02:49:59-08:00","id":1525060,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Supernatural Cultists of the Gods of Chaos [Discussion]","content":"So, was reading the Age of Sigmar Hedonites of Slaanesh Battletome earlier this morning when a Conceptual Logic-Chain struck me; since the CoD exists in an alternate version of our world, then it would make sense that Games Workshop, &amp; thus the Warhammer Settings, would exist in some variety. And since Supernatural beings aren't always the most mentally stable of beings, then it wouldn't be completely unexpected if some of such folks were to start worshipping said deities for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> Thus lies my question/topic proposal for our contemplation in this thread; out of the Four main Chaos Gods of Khorne, Nurgle, Tzeentch &amp; Slaanesh, how would their worship be spread across the various Splats?<br /> <br /> I myself would say that Tzeentch would be the most popular of the four by far amongst those Mages crazy and/or foolish enough to worship him, since, you know, God of Magic &amp; Mystery &amp; all that Jazz. Though Khorne would most definitely be the least liked among the Wise due to the anti-magic elements of his philosophy.<br /> Werewolves are almost complete shoe-ins for Khorne due to his Domains of Battle &amp; Rage, though I wouldn't be too surprised if Slaanesh had a certain level of grip due to the temptation of attaining ever-greater hunting skill.<br /> Vampires Would likely be, on some level, attracted to all four; Khorne since he's a Blood God &amp; they're creatures of Blood, Slaanesh to finally get to actually feel physical sensations again, Tzeentch due to his power over trickery, plans &amp; plotting, &amp; Nurgle to try to preserve their mortal loved ones without Embracing or Ghouling them.<br /> Deviants are <i>way</i> too varied to really say anything for certain, beyond Tzeentch drawing in a large number of Psychics &amp; Mutants, &amp; Nurgle's mastery over nature providing a large draw for Chimerics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T03:18:25-08:00","id":1525061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion#post1525060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...since the CoD exists in an alternate version of our world, then it would make sense that Games Workshop, &amp; thus the Warhammer Settings, would exist in some variety. And since Supernatural beings aren't always the most mentally stable of beings, then it wouldn't be completely unexpected if some of such folks were to start worshipping said deities for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to clarify, your idea isn't to transfer the Chaos Gods over, but instead that a supernatural being would for whatever reason pick up a Games Workshop product, and decide that the deities inside are actually real?<br /> <br /> Sounds like something a Banisher from <i>Awakening</i> might do (there's your Khorne mage). Though honestly, plenty of 'real' occultism is explicit fiction that people have chosen to take as real, so it's not necessarily that unlikely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T07:11:21-08:00","id":1525070,"title":"","content":"A Spirit choir might have latched onto those identities and tried to propagate them as their own, I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T09:56:36-08:00","id":1525075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525070#post1525070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Spirit choir might have latched onto those identities and tried to propagate them as their own, I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where I think I would take the idea. There's lots of ways it could work to, a joy spirit enjoying the competition of the game, or maybe someone worked super hard customizing and painting a particular model and that awoke it's spirit and it began devourering spirits around it. <br /> <br /> You could even have the spirit start a cult and share it's power with the mortals if you are using Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T15:07:48-08:00","id":1525090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525061#post1525061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify, your idea isn't to transfer the Chaos Gods over, but instead that a supernatural being would for whatever reason pick up a Games Workshop product, and decide that the deities inside are actually real?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>origin</i> of the worship of the four doesn't matter, the gist of what I'm trying to ask is what you lot think the general spread of the four's worship amongst the various supernaturals would be.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525061#post1525061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like something a Banisher from <i>Awakening</i> might do (there's your Khorne mage). Though honestly, plenty of 'real' occultism is explicit fiction that people have chosen to take as real, so it's not necessarily that unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but Awakening-Style Banishers aren't your average mage, are they? &amp; I was referencing such in the bit you quoted. Though I shall concede that the worship of Khorne would not be objected to all that much amongst Banishers, at least in an 'Enemy of my Enemy'/Allies of Convenience sort of manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T05:22:15-08:00","id":1525113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerrorCooper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525090#post1525090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <i>origin</i> of the worship of the four doesn't matter, the gist of what I'm trying to ask is what you lot think the general spread of the four's worship amongst the various supernaturals would be.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is, are they actually real in this setting? Because the way you phrased it made it sound like they were still fictional.<br /> <br /> That's important, because a real Chaos God can give it's worshipers stuff in return and have a real influence on the world, and there are going to be plenty of people lining up to worship them. In contrast, a fictional entity doesn't really have any of that, and you're going to be restricted to a very niche group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe, but Awakening-Style Banishers aren't your average mage, are they? </div> </div> </div>No? I mean, I thought that was your idea. Like, normal mages have actual beings of unimaginable power they can worship if they're into that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> At least in 1e, part of what was unique about Banishers was that they'd invent their own wacky ideas about magic and why it had to be destroyed. That's why I suggested them, because you'd need to be pretty odd to walk into a Games Workshop and think that their games are works of theology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T07:56:42-08:00","id":1525119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525113#post1525113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's important, because a real Chaos God can give it's worshipers stuff in return and have a real influence on the world, and there are going to be plenty of people lining up to worship them. In contrast, a fictional entity doesn't really have any of that, and you're going to be restricted to a very niche group.</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter what, if any, religion you believe, odds are you believe that, throughout the history of mankind there have been hundreds, if not thousands, of fictional deities, and those deities have shared between them millions of worshippers across the years, while not actually granting their followers any kind of real influence on the world. <br /> <br /> That said, I don't think this idea is good for much past a side quest type thing, I wouldn't want to play a game in which Warhammer 40k gods were a significant plot point unless I was actually playing Warhammer 40k, but I do think as an aside, kind of a &quot;weird shit happens in the world, here's an example&quot; this could work well. Even in the real world murderers have blamed their actions on physical objects, the Son of Sam being a notable case where he blamed his actions on a dog. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T09:54:17-08:00","id":1525125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525119#post1525119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter what, if any, religion you believe, odds are you believe that, throughout the history of mankind there have been hundreds, if not thousands, of fictional deities, and those deities have shared between them millions of worshippers across the years, while not actually granting their followers any kind of real influence on the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but there's fiction in the sense of untrue, and there's fiction in the sense of being literal intellectual property set around a game of toy soldiers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T12:41:35-08:00","id":1525130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525125#post1525125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure, but there's fiction in the sense of untrue, and there's fiction in the sense of being literal intellectual property set around a game of toy soldiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair. Also allow me to point out that a failed science fiction author once said that if he wanted money he would start a religion. He later did so, basing the religion off of his failed science fiction books. That religion now has 40,000 followers across the world and has performed the largest infiltration of the U.S. Government to date. Another notable instance had involved people being willing to sacrifice themselves for aliens who hid behind a comet. <br /> <br /> All of that is to say that what a person pushing as a belief is often less important than their personal charisma. There's always desperate people willing to believe what a powerful personality tells them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 11-06-2023, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T18:02:42-08:00","id":1525142,"title":"","content":"Most will be changelings and hobgoblins. They\u2019re already empowered by a cosmic force of interconnectivity and relavity where the give-and-take act between actors matters more than who the actors are, and fueled by congealed emotional surges.<br /> <br /> Also, ghosts and the Bound. The Chthonic Gods are already written as gods whose existence is dubious; churches of the dead worshipping the Ruinous Powers as yet another masks of the Chthonic Gods, or similar divinities, isn\u2019t that much out of place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T00:57:16-08:00","id":1525158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525113#post1525113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The point is, are they actually real in this setting? Because the way you phrased it made it sound like they were still fictional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fictional gods in CofD exist as actual Goetia, so the question for them becomes if they can build up actual worshippers and/or reward them with replicating their beliefs.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they are Abyssal creature, as Chaos and the Abyss have some commonalities... Annunkai of Slannesh would be terrible.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T04:05:10-08:00","id":1525202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525113#post1525113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point is, are they actually real in this setting? Because the way you phrased it made it sound like they were still fictional.<br /> <br /> That's important, because a real Chaos God can give it's worshipers stuff in return and have a real influence on the world, and there are going to be plenty of people lining up to worship them. In contrast, a fictional entity doesn't really have any of that, and you're going to be restricted to a very niche group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the ST. 'Sides, it isn't like people haven't worshipped blatantly fictional beings before, like how Shadowcatx pointed out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1525060-supernatural-cultists-of-the-gods-of-chaos-discussion?p=1525113#post1525113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No? I mean, I thought that was your idea. Like, normal mages have actual beings of unimaginable power they can worship if they're into that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> At least in 1e, part of what was unique about Banishers was that they'd invent their own wacky ideas about magic and why it had to be destroyed. That's why I suggested them, because you'd need to be pretty odd to walk into a Games Workshop and think that their games are works of theology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more along the lines of 2e, though I could see a Banisher doing as you described based on what little I know of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T08:43:39-08:00","id":1525208,"title":"","content":"Ultimately the only questions are does the ST allow it and what does the Mystery Cult offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}